{title: Lord As To Thy Dear Cross}
{artist: John Hampden Gurney}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 100}

Verse 1
[Eb]Lord, as [Bb]to [Eb]Thy [Bb7]dear [Ddim]cross [Eb]we [Bb]flee, And [Eb]plead [Cm]to [F7]be for[Bb]giv'n,
So [Eb]let [Ab]Thy [Eb]life [C]our [Fm]pat[Bb7]tern [Eb]be, And [Ddim]form [Eb]our [Fm7]souls [Bb]for [Eb]heav'n.

Verse 2
[Eb]Help us, [Bb]through [Eb]good [Bb7]re[Ddim]port [Eb]and [Bb]ill, Our [Eb]dai[Cm]ly [F7]cross to [Bb]bear:
Like [Eb]Thee, [Ab]to [Eb]do [C]our [Fm]Fa[Bb7]ther's [Eb]will, Our [Ddim]bre[Eb]thren's [Fm7]grief [Bb]to [Eb]share.

Verse 3
[Eb]Let grace [Bb]our [Eb]sel[Bb7]fish[Ddim]ness [Eb]ex[Bb]pel, Our [Eb]earth[Cm]li[F7]ness re[Bb]fine;
And [Eb]kind[Ab]ness [Eb]in [C]our [Fm]bo[Bb7]soms [Eb]dwell, As [Ddim]free [Eb]and [Fm7]true [Bb]as [Eb]Thine.

Verse 4
[Eb]If joy [Bb]shall [Eb]at [Bb7]Thy [Ddim]bid[Eb]ding [Bb]fly, And [Eb]grief's [Cm]dark [F7]day come [Bb]on,
We [Eb]in [Ab]our [Eb]turn [C]would [Fm]meek[Bb7]ly [Eb]cry, "Fa[Ddim]ther, [Eb]Thy [Fm7]will [Bb]be [Eb]done."

Verse 5
[Eb]Kept peace[Bb]ful [Eb]in [Bb7]the [Ddim]midst [Eb]of [Bb]strife, For[Eb]giv[Cm]ing [F7]and for[Bb]giv'n,
O [Eb]may [Ab]we [Eb]lead [C]the [Fm]pil[Bb7]grim's [Eb]life And [Ddim]fol[Eb]low [Fm7]Thee [Bb]to [Eb]heav'n.
